WEBVTT

00:00:03.310 --> 00:00:06.560
So, Torqye has the advantage now?

00:00:07.110 --> 00:00:10.320
Yes, signal flares went up not too long ago.

00:00:10.490 --> 00:00:12.030
It signaled a decisive victory.

00:00:13.110 --> 00:00:15.490
Just how much blood has been spilt?

00:00:16.030 --> 00:00:17.830
Mostly the blood of the Imperials.

00:00:24.790 --> 00:00:27.710
It is likely that the fighting will end soon.

00:00:27.880 --> 00:00:28.920
What's going to happen?

00:00:29.090 --> 00:00:32.720
I expect we'll win the battle in Chielo.

00:00:32.880 --> 00:00:34.220
Yes!

00:00:34.380 --> 00:00:35.970
Nothing is certain yet.

00:00:36.140 --> 00:00:39.010
Who will be getting most commended for this battle?

00:00:39.560 --> 00:00:40.850
I'm sure that person

00:00:41.020 --> 00:00:43.350
will be needing this!

00:00:52.440 --> 00:00:54.240
Hoist your flags!

00:00:56.200 --> 00:00:59.200
As planned, the 9th Division will take the city,

00:00:59.370 --> 00:01:03.120
while the 10th and 11th Divisions will hold off
the Torqyean army.

00:01:03.290 --> 00:01:05.000
We will take down Espada

00:01:05.160 --> 00:01:07.830
and mark the beginning of our counterattack!

00:01:19.100 --> 00:01:26.020
Altair: A Record of Battles

00:02:43.220 --> 00:02:47.060
THE END OF PARADISE

00:03:01.910 --> 00:03:04.530
Once the city falls, we will be victorious!

00:03:04.700 --> 00:03:06.330
The enemies only number a thousand!

00:03:06.490 --> 00:03:09.540
They cannot stop the 9th Division and our 5000 men!

00:03:09.710 --> 00:03:13.080
Bieger and Nohl will hold off the Torqyean army!

00:03:13.250 --> 00:03:15.630
So focus only what is in front of you and march!

00:03:16.170 --> 00:03:18.460
Why are you coming this way?

00:03:18.630 --> 00:03:21.880
If you just surrendered we could all go home early.

00:03:22.800 --> 00:03:26.470
Besides, whoever said
there were only a thousand of us?

00:03:27.010 --> 00:03:29.230
We've got 10,000 mercenaries on our side.

00:03:30.230 --> 00:03:35.270
I told you our client was that group of rich people,

00:03:35.440 --> 00:03:36.980
the Cuore Alliance.

00:03:37.150 --> 00:03:39.940
Even after hiring this many,
we still had money to spare.

00:03:45.870 --> 00:03:47.660
What about you guys?

00:03:47.830 --> 00:03:51.000
If you surrender, I'll even hire you.

00:03:55.250 --> 00:03:57.210
Where could he have gone?

00:03:57.380 --> 00:04:00.470
Do you not have any more ideas?

00:04:00.630 --> 00:04:03.340
If we haven't found him
after all the searching we've done,

00:04:03.550 --> 00:04:06.180
there's only one place I can think of.

00:04:06.390 --> 00:04:08.100
The Tower of Silence.

00:04:10.730 --> 00:04:12.190
Let's go take a look.

00:04:15.400 --> 00:04:17.320
Espada hasn't fallen yet?

00:04:17.480 --> 00:04:19.940
What is Commander Altdorfer doing?

00:04:20.150 --> 00:04:22.900
They have twice as many men
as the 9th Division.

00:04:23.360 --> 00:04:24.700
The city won't fall.

00:04:24.910 --> 00:04:27.240
This was completely our miscalculation.

00:04:27.450 --> 00:04:28.620
Commander Nohl!

00:04:28.790 --> 00:04:31.950
The 11th Division cannot hold any longer!

00:04:32.410 --> 00:04:33.960
It's not too late.

00:04:34.120 --> 00:04:36.750
I will try to convince General Pino to surrender.

00:04:36.880 --> 00:04:38.710
No, Commander Bieger.

00:04:39.460 --> 00:04:40.800
It is too late.

00:04:40.960 --> 00:04:42.420
I leave the rest in your hands!

00:04:42.590 --> 00:04:43.880
Nohl!

00:04:44.050 --> 00:04:47.970
11th Division, taking Espada will not be possible.

00:04:48.140 --> 00:04:50.810
We no longer have a reason to hold back and defend.

00:04:50.970 --> 00:04:54.020
So go out there and give them everything you've got!

00:05:04.200 --> 00:05:05.570
10th Division!

00:05:05.740 --> 00:05:08.990
You will not be coming out of this battle alive!

00:05:09.160 --> 00:05:12.200
If you do not want to die,
you'll have to play dead.

00:05:12.370 --> 00:05:15.670
Prisoners are a desirable commodity for the enemy.

00:05:15.830 --> 00:05:19.130
They're sure to treat you well after the battle is over.

00:05:19.340 --> 00:05:22.630
But if you still want to stick it out with me
despite the odds,

00:05:22.800 --> 00:05:26.800
then stand with me and protect our leader
until the last of us falls!

00:05:28.930 --> 00:05:30.970
All forces, charge!

00:05:38.440 --> 00:05:40.900
Please be there, Director.

00:05:41.070 --> 00:05:42.610
He must be.

00:05:42.780 --> 00:05:45.900
That tower was built to be the final stronghold

00:05:46.070 --> 00:05:49.570
should the enemy break through the walls
in a siege.

00:05:49.740 --> 00:05:53.040
That sounds like the perfect place to hole up
with a hostage.

00:05:53.200 --> 00:05:54.450
Let's hurry.

00:06:02.670 --> 00:06:04.510
Horse archers, fire!

00:06:04.670 --> 00:06:06.170
Ruckenschild!

00:06:09.510 --> 00:06:10.640
Hold!

00:06:12.430 --> 00:06:13.470
Damn it!

00:06:13.680 --> 00:06:16.480
They're free to do whatever they want.

00:06:19.730 --> 00:06:23.440
Damn it! They're charging in!

00:06:25.230 --> 00:06:27.700
It seems like we'll be able to climb the ivy.

00:06:27.860 --> 00:06:29.280
Let's hurry then.

00:06:30.360 --> 00:06:31.870
Let's take it slow.

00:06:32.030 --> 00:06:33.990
He'll pull something off, anyway.

00:06:34.160 --> 00:06:35.660
We can't assume that.

00:06:35.830 --> 00:06:39.040
We need to sort this out before
Mahmut Pasha gets back.

00:06:39.210 --> 00:06:40.750
It was a decisive victory, right?

00:06:41.290 --> 00:06:44.210
-Probably.
-No, it definitely was.

00:06:44.380 --> 00:06:45.550
I can see it.

00:06:45.710 --> 00:06:50.840
See Mahmut Pasha crushing the Imperial soldiers
and slaughtering every last one of them, that is.

00:06:55.180 --> 00:06:56.220
Regroup!

00:06:56.390 --> 00:06:58.600
There's no use! These thin lines are nothing!

00:07:03.730 --> 00:07:05.520
It's war. What choice does he have?

00:07:05.940 --> 00:07:09.450
If he didn't have a choice,
he wouldn't hate war so much.

00:07:09.900 --> 00:07:12.450
He hates war, yet he's strong in battle.

00:07:12.620 --> 00:07:16.290
He kills more soldiers than anyone
while caring most about his people.

00:07:17.200 --> 00:07:18.790
I can see it.

00:07:18.960 --> 00:07:24.540
I can see the countless people that were sacrificed
for his cause gathered behind him.

00:07:33.430 --> 00:07:34.890
General Pino.

00:07:35.050 --> 00:07:41.480
We are the executors of Minister Louis' vision
of expanding our military and territories.

00:07:42.230 --> 00:07:47.780
Minister Louis aimed to establish a thousand years
of prosperity for the Empire with the sword.

00:07:48.150 --> 00:07:50.990
Bringing that about was my dream.

00:07:51.610 --> 00:07:53.070
Which is why

00:07:53.240 --> 00:07:55.870
I must die in despair.

00:07:56.410 --> 00:07:58.910
But your true aim
was to make the Empire a major power

00:07:59.250 --> 00:08:04.000
by enhancing ourselves domestically
without having to rely on invasions.

00:08:05.000 --> 00:08:06.960
Ironically, this defeat

00:08:07.550 --> 00:08:08.960
may help you

00:08:09.420 --> 00:08:11.720
actualize your dream.

00:08:24.440 --> 00:08:26.980
He's a really complicated person,

00:08:27.110 --> 00:08:29.070
full of contradictions.

00:08:30.150 --> 00:08:31.320
Give it a rest already.

00:08:47.080 --> 00:08:50.000
Look, we have killed the Empire's general!

00:08:50.170 --> 00:08:54.180
Victory is ours!

00:09:07.350 --> 00:09:09.820
What terrifying people!

00:09:09.980 --> 00:09:11.230
Cruel and savage,

00:09:11.400 --> 00:09:14.530
bloodthirsty animals whose wickedness
knows no bounds!

00:09:15.150 --> 00:09:16.860
The legend of the Torqyeans

00:09:17.030 --> 00:09:18.990
was all true.

00:09:19.530 --> 00:09:21.040
Oh, woe is me.

00:09:21.240 --> 00:09:24.960
The thought of having to ally
ourselves with such people!

00:09:25.500 --> 00:09:28.380
What? Oh, no! One of them is coming this way!

00:09:29.250 --> 00:09:31.840
Lince! Well fought!

00:09:32.000 --> 00:09:35.630
This victory would not have been possible
without your help.

00:09:35.800 --> 00:09:40.100
What? He's got a wolf on his shoulder.

00:09:40.260 --> 00:09:43.390
Lince deserves the most credit for this battle.

00:09:43.560 --> 00:09:47.520
Therefore, the spoils of this battle
including the prisoners and weapons...

00:09:47.690 --> 00:09:49.560
What is that? Is it alive or dead?

00:09:49.730 --> 00:09:52.480
We would like all of it to go to Lince.

00:09:53.070 --> 00:09:55.860
What? Really?

00:09:56.030 --> 00:10:00.570
There's nothing a troop looks forward to more
than divvying up the spoils of war!

00:10:00.740 --> 00:10:03.990
And you're okay with just letting us take all of it?

00:10:04.160 --> 00:10:05.790
There is no need to worry!

00:10:05.960 --> 00:10:07.870
The economic scale of the Torqye Pashalu

00:10:08.040 --> 00:10:10.750
is far greater than all of the nations
of Cuore combined!

00:10:10.920 --> 00:10:14.460
We will be able to give our soldiers ample reward
on their return.

00:10:14.630 --> 00:10:19.140
Torqye knows how to treat the allies
who protect our backs.

00:10:19.680 --> 00:10:23.600
Please take care of Espada until this war is over.

00:10:28.560 --> 00:10:30.270
Good work, men.

00:10:30.440 --> 00:10:34.480
We will make camp here once the spoils of battle
have been distributed.

00:10:34.730 --> 00:10:36.490
Mahmut Pasha...

00:10:37.240 --> 00:10:40.030
However, this is not the end of our battle.

00:10:40.530 --> 00:10:44.410
Many thousands of people are waiting
for our return in Chielo.

00:10:44.580 --> 00:10:46.790
Once we are rested,

00:10:46.950 --> 00:10:48.330
we will head to Chielo.

00:11:08.100 --> 00:11:09.140
What?

00:11:09.310 --> 00:11:12.940
You ran into an alliance ambush,
and lost half your forces?

00:11:13.480 --> 00:11:18.780
Yes, General Pino is leading the remaining four divisions
towards Espada!

00:11:18.940 --> 00:11:22.700
No, he was forced to head towards Espada.

00:11:22.870 --> 00:11:24.530
There is no saving them now.

00:11:24.700 --> 00:11:26.120
Frentzen.

00:11:26.290 --> 00:11:31.210
I doubt that there is any part of you that considers
going to save General Pino an option.

00:11:31.370 --> 00:11:32.750
You're right, Adam.

00:11:32.920 --> 00:11:36.380
We cannot afford to lose what little men we have.

00:11:37.760 --> 00:11:40.340
We are withdrawing our troops from Chielo.

00:11:43.510 --> 00:11:44.760
We've been found!

00:11:44.930 --> 00:11:47.350
What did you say?
What are we going to do, Augusto?

00:11:47.510 --> 00:11:49.600
Most of our people have been caught.

00:11:49.770 --> 00:11:51.520
We'll be killed if they get inside!

00:11:52.060 --> 00:11:54.730
We're doing all this to save the city!

00:11:54.900 --> 00:11:56.230
Why are they doing this?

00:11:59.360 --> 00:12:01.320
Man, he's fast.

00:12:01.490 --> 00:12:04.110
This is all about physical strength.

00:12:04.280 --> 00:12:05.620
See you later!

00:12:05.780 --> 00:12:07.200
You little!

00:12:08.910 --> 00:12:10.290
Ow!

00:12:11.620 --> 00:12:13.080
Huh?

00:12:25.510 --> 00:12:28.060
You could've killed us!
What's wrong with you?

00:12:28.220 --> 00:12:29.930
I got hit by a rock.

00:12:30.100 --> 00:12:31.350
What?

00:12:35.520 --> 00:12:37.310
What are you doing?

00:12:37.480 --> 00:12:39.110
Grandma?

00:12:39.280 --> 00:12:42.650
Perren, Achilles, even you too, Valentine?

00:12:42.820 --> 00:12:45.160
Is this a joke? What are you doing?

00:12:45.860 --> 00:12:49.830
I found her cold this morning.

00:12:49.990 --> 00:12:52.000
My grandfather died last night.

00:12:52.160 --> 00:12:54.080
My younger brother is going to die.

00:12:54.210 --> 00:12:56.170
This is not what you told us would happen!

00:12:56.710 --> 00:12:58.630
We can't go on like this anymore!

00:12:58.790 --> 00:13:01.260
Venedik isn't coming!

00:13:01.420 --> 00:13:05.720
And the great Torqyean Pasha hasn't come back
after saying he would go defeat the Empire!

00:13:05.880 --> 00:13:08.140
You saw the victory flares go up this morning!

00:13:08.300 --> 00:13:09.760
Like we could trust that!

00:13:09.930 --> 00:13:11.140
Augusto!

00:13:11.310 --> 00:13:12.600
You can see for yourself!

00:13:12.770 --> 00:13:14.770
We're on your side too!

00:13:15.350 --> 00:13:19.020
We'll do anything to save this city.

00:13:19.230 --> 00:13:23.530
Our only option is to hand the director
to the Empire and surrender.

00:13:23.940 --> 00:13:25.860
Thank you for your support!

00:13:27.780 --> 00:13:32.870
We will now execute Director Carbajal
for defying the Empire!

00:13:36.040 --> 00:13:39.080
Do it, Augusto! Kill him!

00:13:39.250 --> 00:13:40.500
You ingrate!

00:13:40.710 --> 00:13:42.670
How could you say that?

00:13:42.840 --> 00:13:45.260
You did it now, you damn Ninan refugee!

00:13:46.180 --> 00:13:48.090
If you didn't come here,

00:13:48.260 --> 00:13:49.930
we would've had plenty of food!

00:13:50.100 --> 00:13:51.600
What did you say?

00:13:51.760 --> 00:13:52.930
Stop.

00:13:53.970 --> 00:13:57.350
This is not a matter you Ninan refugees
need to concern yourself with.

00:13:57.560 --> 00:14:02.900
Every citizen of Chielo is either a former refugee
who found salvation in this city

00:14:03.070 --> 00:14:04.150
or their descendants.

00:14:05.360 --> 00:14:08.820
Even my own grandfather,
who long ago lost everything in war,

00:14:09.030 --> 00:14:11.080
was saved by this city

00:14:11.240 --> 00:14:13.370
when he was on the verge of death.

00:14:13.540 --> 00:14:16.830
My grandfather was able to die in peace,

00:14:17.000 --> 00:14:19.540
grateful to this city for what it's done.

00:14:21.840 --> 00:14:23.960
So even if it happens

00:14:24.170 --> 00:14:26.760
that I die of starvation today,

00:14:26.920 --> 00:14:30.890
I will never regret inviting these people into our city.

00:14:31.430 --> 00:14:33.850
Casandra! Thank you!

00:14:34.390 --> 00:14:38.310
That means so much to me and this city.

00:14:38.850 --> 00:14:42.770
And all of you need to stop fighting among friends.

00:14:46.940 --> 00:14:48.860
No matter what happens now,

00:14:49.070 --> 00:14:51.740
please let them go.

00:14:53.450 --> 00:14:57.370
That's because we all already have the key to heaven.

00:14:58.080 --> 00:14:59.750
Key to heaven?

00:14:59.920 --> 00:15:01.250
From the play?

00:15:01.420 --> 00:15:04.630
In order to get to the eternal paradise of Chielo.

00:15:04.800 --> 00:15:07.090
Even if for one moment in your life,

00:15:07.260 --> 00:15:10.720
you felt glad for being born,

00:15:12.430 --> 00:15:16.560
then people will be able
to die thankful for their lives.

00:15:18.180 --> 00:15:23.190
There is no greater final feliz than to be able
to die thankful for your life.

00:15:23.730 --> 00:15:25.940
It's just like reaching Chielo.

00:15:26.320 --> 00:15:28.650
Having lived a life you can be proud of,

00:15:28.820 --> 00:15:31.070
or leaving behind a masterpiece,

00:15:31.240 --> 00:15:33.070
or having met a wonderful person,

00:15:33.240 --> 00:15:36.200
it doesn't matter what your reasons are
to be thankful.

00:15:36.740 --> 00:15:41.920
I always wanted to be one of those reasons for you.

00:15:43.750 --> 00:15:47.300
But I failed completely.

00:15:48.590 --> 00:15:51.090
You are making the right choice.

00:15:53.340 --> 00:15:56.220
Now, Augusto, Salomon.

00:15:56.760 --> 00:15:58.350
I pray that my death will at least

00:15:58.520 --> 00:16:02.690
lead to your final feliz.

00:16:03.400 --> 00:16:05.110
Casandra!

00:16:06.900 --> 00:16:08.480
I leave the rest to you.

00:16:08.650 --> 00:16:10.690
Do it, Salomon!

00:16:10.860 --> 00:16:11.860
Stop!

00:16:12.360 --> 00:16:14.740
The war is already ending!

00:16:36.800 --> 00:16:39.260
Take him to the Empire and surrender!

00:16:41.180 --> 00:16:44.560
What are you doing? If you don't hurry,
the Empire is going to attack!

00:16:44.730 --> 00:16:46.020
Silence!

00:16:53.950 --> 00:16:57.320
This is the will of the people of Chielo.

00:17:00.620 --> 00:17:02.410
Withdraw immediately?

00:17:02.620 --> 00:17:04.330
What are you talking about, Frentzen?

00:17:04.460 --> 00:17:07.630
If Chielo learns of our retreat,

00:17:07.790 --> 00:17:10.050
they will surely pursue after us!

00:17:10.210 --> 00:17:11.920
We should wait until dark!

00:17:12.090 --> 00:17:14.090
Then it will be too late.

00:17:14.260 --> 00:17:15.470
Don't worry.

00:17:15.630 --> 00:17:18.260
We'll be able to handle a mere militia.

00:17:18.430 --> 00:17:20.390
Don't underestimate a contested retreat.

00:17:20.560 --> 00:17:22.220
How very sad.

00:17:22.390 --> 00:17:25.980
Who was the one proclaiming that I was the Prophet?

00:17:26.140 --> 00:17:28.400
This isn't time for jokes.

00:17:28.560 --> 00:17:30.270
Why are you rushing our departure?

00:17:30.440 --> 00:17:32.820
The Torqyeans won't be here
until tomorrow morning.

00:17:32.990 --> 00:17:37.160
There will be someone who will arrive here sooner
than the Torqyeans, remember?

00:17:37.320 --> 00:17:39.910
Commander Frentzen!
I have a report from our scouts.

00:17:40.080 --> 00:17:44.710
An estimated 5000 El Toro cavalrymen from the alliance
are currently advancing towards Chielo.

00:17:44.870 --> 00:17:46.960
Their estimated time of arrival is sundown!

00:17:47.620 --> 00:17:50.710
Is there something you'd like to say, Adam?

00:17:50.880 --> 00:17:53.590
I'm sorry, My Lord Prophet.

00:17:54.840 --> 00:17:57.800
All forces, begin our retreat!

00:18:02.010 --> 00:18:03.100
Hey!

00:18:04.430 --> 00:18:07.140
The Imperial army! The Imperial army...

00:18:07.690 --> 00:18:10.440
The Imperial army is retreating!

00:18:43.510 --> 00:18:45.470
Who is at fault?

00:18:45.640 --> 00:18:48.270
Everyone is both a victim and a perpetrator.

00:18:48.850 --> 00:18:50.730
Who will you blame?

00:18:50.900 --> 00:18:53.270
Who can you blame, Mahmut?

00:19:00.320 --> 00:19:01.740
It is truly unfortunate,

00:19:01.910 --> 00:19:04.580
for him to die in vain like this.

00:19:05.200 --> 00:19:07.620
I appreciate your sentiment.

00:19:07.750 --> 00:19:12.330
However, the Director did not die in vain.

00:19:13.210 --> 00:19:16.590
We had no idea what the situation was outside!

00:19:16.760 --> 00:19:20.590
We thought the only way to save Chielo
was to surrender to the Empire!

00:19:20.760 --> 00:19:23.010
Can you blame us for thinking that?

00:19:23.180 --> 00:19:26.220
-What are you talking about?
-You all killed the Director!

00:19:26.390 --> 00:19:27.560
That is enough.

00:19:29.600 --> 00:19:33.690
Please remember the words Director Carbajal left us.

00:19:33.860 --> 00:19:37.650
We already possess the key to heaven.

00:19:38.110 --> 00:19:39.990
I, too, believe that.

00:19:40.530 --> 00:19:45.030
You all had started to fight amongst yourselves,

00:19:45.370 --> 00:19:49.000
but you stopped because of the director's words.

00:19:49.540 --> 00:19:52.790
You all possess the capacity for reason.

00:19:52.920 --> 00:19:55.540
Let us stop blaming Augusto.

00:19:57.550 --> 00:20:00.050
We must accept the director's death.

00:20:02.550 --> 00:20:07.430
This country is a gathering of people who cannot survive
these troubled times on their own.

00:20:08.850 --> 00:20:11.440
But even people like them

00:20:11.600 --> 00:20:16.480
deserve to have at least one place where they can live
and die in peace, don't they?

00:20:20.990 --> 00:20:23.200
We must protect it ourselves.

00:20:23.360 --> 00:20:26.450
Let us take the words the director has left to us,

00:20:26.620 --> 00:20:29.200
and make Chielo the best it can be.

00:20:34.460 --> 00:20:35.710
Casandra.

00:20:36.460 --> 00:20:42.090
But I still don't believe Chielo's people
are capable of holding the city on their own.

00:20:42.840 --> 00:20:43.930
I understand.

00:20:44.090 --> 00:20:48.640
It is only natural for someone in your position
to come to that assessment.

00:20:49.560 --> 00:20:54.100
The anti-Imperial Alliance shall take sovereignty
over the Republic of Chielo.

00:20:54.850 --> 00:20:56.520
Understood.

00:20:57.110 --> 00:20:59.270
But I am not upset.

00:20:59.860 --> 00:21:02.240
I believe that the day will come

00:21:02.740 --> 00:21:08.030
when the people of Chielo can get back on our feet
and gain the understanding of the allied nations.

00:21:08.200 --> 00:21:09.700
I look forward to it.

00:21:19.710 --> 00:21:21.090
You got that right!

00:21:21.250 --> 00:21:22.710
We're at war,

00:21:22.880 --> 00:21:25.510
and they don't even know what line not to cross?

00:21:25.680 --> 00:21:28.600
Mahmut's not going to stay quiet on this one!

00:21:28.760 --> 00:21:34.140
While we're at it, I've got a thing or two to say
to the noticeably absent Venedik too.

00:21:34.350 --> 00:21:35.810
It is worrisome.

00:21:35.980 --> 00:21:38.770
They should be heading here directly this time.

00:21:39.900 --> 00:21:41.480
Mahmut.

00:21:41.650 --> 00:21:46.490
You are forced to move forward in the face
of many obstacles.

00:21:46.910 --> 00:21:48.990
What are you mumbling about?

00:21:49.160 --> 00:21:53.080
El Toro has great respect for those with strength.

00:21:53.250 --> 00:21:56.080
Even if you cause nothing but trouble,

00:21:56.210 --> 00:21:58.290
I'll still follow you.

00:22:03.460 --> 00:22:07.090
June 30th, Torqyean Calendar Year 76

00:22:07.800 --> 00:22:12.720
The 15,000 Imperial soldiers sieging Chielo
withdrew from the city.

00:23:48.990 --> 00:23:50.860
What do I know?

00:23:51.150 --> 00:23:52.490
About this country.

00:23:52.780 --> 00:23:53.990
About war.

00:23:54.200 --> 00:23:56.030
About what I must do.

00:23:56.950 --> 00:23:58.450
Next time, "Instigation."

00:23:59.040 --> 00:24:00.830
Let's go, Iskandar.
